    "fileId": 53,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p><strong>Box&nbsp;14.05</strong> Diagnostic criteria for juvenile polyposis syndrome {1656892; 2853131}</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "source error",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"601\">\r\n<p>1. &gt;&nbsp;3&ndash;5&nbsp;juvenile polyps of the colorectum</p>\r\n<p>2. Juvenile polyps throughout the GI tract</p>\r\n<p>3. Any number of juvenile polyps with a family history of juvenile polyposis</p>\r\n<p>Other syndromes involving hamartomatous gastrointestinal polyps should be ruled out clinically or by pathological examination.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p></p>",
